window.bookSummaryJSON = "<b>Baby Keller is the most beautiful woman in the world.</b><br><br>I hate that name: Baby. So harmless—such a misdirection. A lie. But I’m not sure what else I should’ve expected from a Keller....<br><br>Hunter Black and Baby Keller are enemies--tried and true, sealed in hatred.<br><br>And desire. Because she has never been so surprised by herself, and he has never been so quick to want a woman--and never the way he wants her.<br><br>Now the Ashwood Society has plans for them both. Caught in their web, they can only fight their way out together--or not at all.<br><br>TRIGGER WARNING: Violence, some of it sexual, appears in this book. Not that any of these books are a walk in the park, but this is a big warning to please pick up another book to read if these things upset you. Dark dark days ahead.<br><br>Love. Betrayal. And magic. Welcome to the world of the Ashwood Institute, where witches and monsters are as devastatingly real as the hearts they break. Dark, erotic, devious and addictive, the Legends of the Ashwood Institute Series begins with DARE ME and continues in the following order:<br>DARE ME<br>DENY ME <br>ENSLAVE ME <br>DEFY ME<br>ENCHANT ME<br>CURSE ME<br><br>This book is NOT meant for a young adult audience--it is meant for adults and contains content for adults. It is NOT a stand-alone; if you hate cliff-hangers, this is NOT the book for you. It overlaps with the following genres: paranormal, dark, contemporary, and college/new adult romance and romantic suspense/thriller/mystery."; 
